audit_conclusions:
- Slice D is input plumbing only.
- ArchitectPlanContextPacket enters Gemini Architect input only under explicit gate.
- The new Architect packet input gate alone does not start Gemini.
- Existing Gemini Architect mode without the new gate is unchanged.
- ArchitectPlanContextPacket is validated before provider dispatch.
- Validation failure blocks provider before model/network/Gemini call.
- ArchitectPlanContextPacket is not execution authority.
- Architect is not Root.
- Architect does not create ActionCommitPacket.
- Plan packet is not execution authority.
- ContextPacket is not truth.
- ContextPacket is not authority.
- ContextPacket is not action permission.
- ContextPacket is not FinalOutput.
- ContextPacket is not ActionCommitPacket.
- Gemini proposes, Root disposes.
- Root remains final authority.
- Dual path now consumes both OrchestratorRouteContextPacket and ArchitectPlanContextPacket.
- Architect still consumes validated route as before.
- No raw cross-role text.
- No default output shape drift.
- No counter drift.
- No stage_map drift.
- No production/public WOW claim.
- No NeedleFactory/Marennya/UP.
- Ready for Dual Rich Context smoke / next rationale layer only after this audit is committed.

verdict:
- Rich Context / Bounded Context Packets Slice D accepted as gated Gemini Architect input plumbing.
- The packet input preserves Root authority and leaves PlanGraph runtime, AVF, DRS, GT/LGT, and Root behavior unchanged.
- Root remains final authority.
